          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+functor"} topological functor
                is solid. Indeed, a functor
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                is topological just when it has final lifts for all
                = succeed "-structured" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                %em final lift
                is a semi-final lift for which
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
                is an isomorphism.
            %li
              %p
                Any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monadic+functor"} monadic functor
                into
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
                is solid.
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fully+faithful+functor"} fully faithful functor
                is solid if and only if it has a left adjoint.
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\colon A\to X
                is faithful and has a left adjoint, and moreover
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete+category"} cocomplete
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well-powered+category"} well-copowered
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                is solid.
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated model category
                with monic generating cofibrations, the forgetful functor from
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+algebraic+fibrant+objects"} algebraic fibrant objects
                to
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is solid. See there for details.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#left_adjoint Left adjoint
          %p
            For any
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            is a
            = succeed "-structured" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/adjoint+functor#UniversalArrows"} universal arrow
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\to U b
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is solid, then it has a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
          %h3#lifting_of_colimits Lifting of colimits
          %p
            Suppose that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\colon A\to X
            is solid and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon D\to A
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U F
            has a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocone"} cocone
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mi F
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U F d_i \to c
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \to U e
            be a semi-final lift of this
            = succeed "-structured" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi i
                  %mo →
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F d_i \to e
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is faithful, these morphisms are a cocone under
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            Therefore, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is solid over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            does. Moreover, if we understand colimits in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %p
            In particular, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete+category"} cocomplete
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+category"} total
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %h3#lifting_of_model_structures Lifting of model structures
          %p
            The standard
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transferred+model+structure"} transfer theorem
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model structures
            states that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\colon A\to X
            is a functor such that
          %ol
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              has a left adjoint
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+functor"} accessible
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
              for sufficiently large
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi κ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              has a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated model structure
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+composition"} Transfinite composites
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushouts"} pushouts
              of images under
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              of generating acyclic cofibrations in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              become weak equivalences after applying
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              (the
              = succeed ")," do
                %em acyclicity condition
          %p
            then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            has a cofibrantly generated model structure in which the weak equivalences and fibrations are created by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Nikolaus"} Nikolaus
          #LiftingTheorem.un_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\colon A\to X
              be an accessible solid functor, and assume that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              has a cofibrantly generated model structure and the following acyclicity condition:
            %ul
              %li
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi D
                      %mo →
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F\colon D\to A
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+diagram"} filtered diagram
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(F(d_i)) \to x
                is a cocone under
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U\circ F
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi X
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\to U(b)
                of this
                = succeed "-structured" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %p
              Then the transfer theorem applies, so that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              has a cofibrantly generated model structure in which the weak equivalences and fibrations are created by
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              We have remarked above that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              has a left adjoint, and we assumed it to be accessible, so it remains to show that the given acyclicity condition implies the standard one.
            %p
              We first show that
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              of images under
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              of generating acyclic cofibrations become acyclic cofibrations (not just weak equivalences) upon applying
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi x
                    %mo →
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i\colon x\to y
              be a generating acyclic cofibration, and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo
                              %mrow
                                %mi F
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi i
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{F(x) &amp; \overset{f}{\to} &amp; a\\
                    ^{F (i)}\downarrow \\
                    F(y)}
            %p
              a diagram in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              of which we would like to take the pushout. Consider the pushout of the corresponding diagram in
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi x
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mover
                                %mi f
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                              %mi g
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi y
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mi h
                          %mtd
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msub
                              %mo ⊔
                              %mi x
                            %mi y
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{x &amp; \overset{\bar{f}}{\to} &amp; U(a)\\
                    ^{i}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow^g\\
                    y&amp; \underset{h}{\to} &amp; U(a) \sqcup_{x} y.}
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a model category,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              is an acyclic cofibration. Therefore, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mi x
                    %mi y
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi k
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(a) \sqcup_x y \overset{k}{\to} U(b)
              is a semifinal lift of the singleton sink
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{g\}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              is also an acyclic cofibration and thus so is the composite
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi a
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi b
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(a)\to U(b)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo →
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\to b
              of which this is the image (which exists by assumption) gives a pushout diagram in
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo
                              %mrow
                                %mi F
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi i
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo →
                              %mover
                                %mi h
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                          %mtd
                            %mi b
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{F(x) &amp; \overset{f}{\to} &amp; a\\
                    ^{F(i)}\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow\\
                    F(y) &amp; \underset{\bar{h}}{\to} &amp; b.}
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is not just accessible but
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitary+functor"} finitary
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              maps to a transfinite composite in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              are acyclic cofibrations, so the desired acyclicity condition follows. In general, we can argue as follows: given a transfinite sequence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi …
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_0\to a_1\to\dots
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              of such pushouts, its colimit (= composition) can be constructed as above by forgetting down to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              are closed under transfinite composites, the legs of the colimiting cocone in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              are acyclic cofibrations. Hence by the assumed acyclicity condition, so is the semifinal lift, and hence (by composition) so are the images in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              of the legs of the colimiting cone in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Walter+Tholen"}> Walter Tholen
                ,
                %em Semitopological functors. I
            %li
              %p and others…
          %p
            The example of algebraic fibrant objects and the argument entering the above
            %a{:href => "#LiftingTheorem"} lifting theorem
            appears in
          %ul#Nikolaus
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Thomas+Nikolaus"}> Thomas Nikolaus
              ,
              %em Algebraic models for higher categories
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1003.1342"}> arXiv
              )
          %p
            See also
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+algebraic+fibrant+objects"} model structure on algebraic fibrant objects
